{
  "_about": [
    "Domain term variants for query expansion (LexiconRewriter) and for authoring",
    "golden questions that exercise vocabulary mismatch.",
    "",
    "Two axes matter in this corpus:",
    "  1. Sanskrit <-> English  (Surya / Sun, bhava / house)",
    "  2. diacritic <-> ASCII   (Surya vs Surya without macrons)",
    "Axis 2 is not cosmetic. The chunks.ts column is to_tsvector('english', text),",
    "which keeps diacritics in the lexeme, so an ASCII query cannot match the",
    "accented corpus form. Measured on 109,163 chunks: 'Surya' (diacritic) matches",
    "16,432 chunks and plain 'Surya' matches 230; 'Mrityubhaga' matches 0 against",
    "183 for the accented form. Expanding the query is the cheap fix; installing",
    "unaccent and rebuilding the generated ts column is the deeper one."
  ],
